# Pin exact minimum source identities for `Simpsons.exe` and `Simpsons.ico`

The source manifest must express exact root-file identities in addition to
folder/type minimums. `Simpsons.exe` and `Simpsons.ico` are mandatory;
`uninst.ico` is explicitly optional and only relevant to some from-scratch
source/build workflows.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Require root `Simpsons.exe` by exact case-sensitive/canonical identity,
  minimum one.
- [x] Require root `Simpsons.ico` by exact canonical identity, minimum one.
- [x] Record root `uninst.ico` as optional with minimum zero.
- [x] Make these requirements immutable schema authority rather than editable
  rows that can turn invalid source into valid source by lowering a count.
- [x] Keep deep deterministic validation authoritative; this exact-file check is
  an early source gate, not a replacement for the reconstruction algorithm.
- [x] Update README source-validation language when implementation lands.

## Dependencies

Coordinate with the canonical game-manifest validator and build preflight.

## Evidence

`game/manifest/game.jsonl` now uses ledger schema v2 with immutable
`required_files` entries for `Simpsons.exe` (minimum 1), `Simpsons.ico`
(minimum 1), and `uninst.ico` (minimum 0). Exact identities are removed from
generic extension counting, so the optional uninstall icon cannot satisfy the
canonical game-icon requirement.

`cargo test -p game_manifest` passed the complete manifest crate suite. Focused
path-helper coverage proves exact casing is required and absence of `uninst.ico`
is accepted. The local canonical `game/` installation then passed
`validate-game` with all 110 generic folder/type minimums plus exact-file
evidence.
